.\" Manual page for LinuxDevStackBox.
.TH LINUXDEVSTACKBOX 1 "October 2026" "0.1.25" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linuxdevstackbox \- local PHP development environment for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linuxdevstackbox
.RI [ option ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B linuxdevstackbox
is a desktop application that manages Apache, MySQL/MariaDB, PHP and
phpMyAdmin for local PHP development. Runtimes come from the distribution
packages; the application generates per-user configuration under the XDG
directories (~/.config/linuxdevstackbox and
~/.local/share/linuxdevstackbox), runs all services as the logged-in user,
and never requires root for normal operation.
.PP
Apache is served from http://localhost:8080/ by default and phpMyAdmin
from http://localhost:8080/phpmyadmin/. The MySQL/MariaDB server listens
on 127.0.0.1:3306 with its socket and data directory under the XDG data
root.
.SH OPTIONS
The graphical application takes no arguments beyond the privileged helper
modes below, which are invoked through
.BR pkexec (1)
by the application itself and are not intended for direct use:
.TP
.B \-\-hosts\-operation add|remove <domain>
Edit the managed /etc/hosts block for a .test hostname.
.TP
.B \-\-ca\-trust\-operation install|remove
Install or remove the local HTTPS CA anchor in the system trust store.
.TP
.B \-\-setup\-local\-https
Provision the local HTTPS certificates non-interactively.
.TP
.B \-\-https\-status
Print the local HTTPS status as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-start\-services, \-\-stop\-services
Start or stop the managed Apache and MySQL services headlessly.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/linuxdevstackbox
Generated configuration (httpd.conf, my.cnf, php.ini, site records,
HTTPS certificates).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/linuxdevstackbox
Runtime data (logs, MySQL data, www projects, backups, phpMyAdmin copy).
Both roots can be redirected with LINUXDEVSTACKBOX_DATA_DIR.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/linuxdevstackbox
Read-only application resources, including the bundled phpMyAdmin.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LINUXDEVSTACKBOX_DATA_DIR
Overrides the XDG config and data roots for the application process.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Service logs are written under ~/.local/share/linuxdevstackbox/logs and
shown on the application's Logs pages.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR httpd (8),
.BR mariadbd (8),
.BR php (1),
.BR pkexec (1)
